  "verbalization": "Omeprazole is implicated in the development of Duodenal Ulcer (disease) through a chain of indications that involve gastric ulceration and subsequent treatment with other drugs. The evidence suggests that Omeprazole is linked to Gastric Ulcer (disease), which in turn is associated with Dexrabeprazole and Duodenal Ulcer (disease), and also with Aluminum Hydroxide and Duodenal Ulcer (disease). This indicates that Omeprazole may contribute to the pathogenesis of Duodenal Ulcer through mechanisms involving gastric acid suppression or irritation. The indirect pathway through Vonoprazan and Dexrabeprazole suggests that Omeprazole may influence gastric function in a way that could lead to ulceration, which is then treated with other drugs that further contribute to the development of Duodenal Ulcer. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role of Omeprazole in the development of Duodenal Ulcer, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
